That's an issue with quite all objects, magical or otherwise overly
useful. So in RL I probably abstain from wishing for objects that I
have to carefully keep with me to be useful.

The Staff would be very nice with it's healing property; presuming
it would heal any disease and injury. That would probably be a wise
choice. But what if you're hit by a car and the staff is at home?
And it would only be wise if it wouldn't have that offensive drain
life property, which would make it a target of theft.

From a practical POV any bag would be nice, because I could stuff
in all the items that require so much store room. :-)  A plain old
sack, or maybe oilskin, is probably better than a bag holding which
might, because of its magic power, be more likely target of theft.

Reflecting about the whole posted list I think I'd go for a blessed
potion of gain ability. (And I'd quaff it immediately, of course.)
Chances are quite low that I'd get any "You're already as strong/
smart/wise/agile/tough/charismatic as you can get." message. ;-)

